# A variable rate mortgage where the payment
# stays the same when the rate moves. Many
# Canadian variable mortgages work this way: a
# rate rise means less of each payment goes to
# the principal, so the loan takes longer to pay
# off. If the rate rises far enough, the payment
# only covers the interest. That rate is the
# trigger rate. The rates are an example path,
# not a forecast.

mortgage "Payment adjusts"
  balance $400,000
  rate 4.2% then 5.5% after 6 months
  amortization 25 years
  term 3 years

scenario "Payment held"
  rate 4.2% then 5.5% after 6 months payment held

compare by payment, interest, balance, payoff, trigger rate
    over 3 years
show trigger rate of "Payment held"
explain "Payment held"

# At renewal the payment is worked out again
# over the amortization that is left.
scenario "Fixed, then renews"
  rate 4.2% then 5.5% after 6 months payment held
  renews at 5%
show renewal payment of "Fixed, then renews"

# How far can the rate rise after 6 months before
# the fixed payment stops covering the interest?
check trigger rate of "Payment held" > 5.5%
